@node View Movement
@subsection View Movement
@cindex thing motion

@deffn Command beads-thing-forward
Move to the next thing, wrapping at the end and echoing @samp{Wrapped}.
Bound to @kbd{TAB}.
@end deffn

@deffn Command beads-thing-backward
Move to the previous thing, wrapping at the beginning.  Bound to
@kbd{S-TAB}.
@end deffn

@deffn Command beads-thing-toggle
Run the thing's own toggle (fold, preview) and then the buffer-local
@code{beads-thing-toggle-functions}.  Bound to @kbd{SPC}.
@end deffn

In a tabulated list every row is a thing.  In section buffers the thing is
a run of text carrying the @code{beads-thing} property.  @kbd{n} and
@kbd{p} move to the next and previous line without wrapping.

@node Pagination
@subsection Pagination
@cindex pagination

@deffn Command beads-pager-mode
Minor mode that sizes a page to the window (with a floor of five rows) and
adds navigation for large result sets.
@end deffn

@table @kbd
@item ]
Move to the next page.
@item [
Move to the previous page.
@item G
Jump to a page.
@item g
Refresh the current view.
@end table

The pagination core is reusable and buffer-agnostic; it is documented
alongside the other extension points.

@node Eldoc Previews
@section Eldoc Previews
@cindex eldoc
@cindex issue previews

@deffn Command beads-eldoc-mode
Toggle hover previews of issue references in the current buffer.
@end deffn

@vindex beads-issue-id-regexp
@vindex beads-issue-id-prefixes
Hover over an issue reference anywhere in Emacs --- a comment, a commit
message, an Org file --- and eldoc previews the issue asynchronously.  The
command is @code{beads-eldoc-mode}; enable it in the buffers where you
want previews.  Issue ids are matched with the shared
@code{beads-issue-id-regexp} and restricted by
@code{beads-issue-id-prefixes}.

Preview data is cached per store, including negative results, so a
reference to an unknown id does not re-query on every keystroke.  Remote
stores are supported; previews use the same asynchronous path as the board
and never block.
